# Web Patterns

## Component Composition

### Compound Components

Use compound components when related UI shares state and interaction semantics:

```tsx
<Tabs defaultValue="overview">
  <Tabs.List>
    <Tabs.Trigger value="overview">Overview</Tabs.Trigger>
    <Tabs.Trigger value="settings">Settings</Tabs.Trigger>
  </Tabs.List>
  <Tabs.Content value="overview">...</Tabs.Content>
  <Tabs.Content value="settings">...</Tabs.Content>
</Tabs>
```

- Parent owns state
- Children consume via context
- Prefer this over prop drilling for complex widgets

### Render Props / Slots

- Use render props or slot patterns when behavior is shared but markup must vary
- Keep keyboard handling, ARIA, and focus logic in the headless layer

### Container / Presentational Split

- Container components own data loading and side effects
- Presentational components receive props and render UI
- Presentational components should stay pure

## State Management

Treat these separately:

| Concern | Tooling |
|---------|---------|
| GraphQL queries, pages, facets, aggregates, detail | Apollo Client cache |
| Live connection state (`lastEventId`, `pendingUpdates`) | Zustand (redux middleware) |
| Local interaction | Component hooks |
| Shareable filters/sorts/time range/cursor | React Router search params |
| Preferences | Context + versioned local storage |
| Filtering, sorting, search, facets, aggregation, export | ClickHouse behind gateway GraphQL |

- Do not duplicate the full corpus into client stores; the browser holds only
  bounded pages from the `findings` connection and live event state
- Derive values instead of storing redundant computed state
- Do not introduce a second remote-state library beside Apollo for GraphQL

## URL As State

Persist shareable state in the URL:
- filters
- sort order
- pagination when it is part of the shareable view contract
- search query when the product contract makes it shareable

## Data Fetching

### Stale-While-Revalidate

- Return cached data immediately
- Revalidate in the background
- Prefer existing libraries instead of rolling this by hand

### Parallel Loading

- Fetch independent data in parallel
- Avoid parent-child request waterfalls
- Prefetch likely next routes or states when justified

## Query, Live, and Detail Loading

Load Explore and Overview from bounded GraphQL queries (`findings` cursor
connection, `facets`, `vulnerabilityOverview`, `datasetInfo`) with `fetchMore`
under the virtualizer. Open `EventSource('/api/stream')` on the main thread
through the `useDatasetEvents` hook; apply `finding-upserted` to the Apollo
cache, treat `findings-changed` and `aggregates-invalidated` as bounded
refetch triggers, and handle `resync-required` by refetching active queries.
Fetch Record Detail lazily through `finding(id)` when a row is selected.
Browser code never decodes protobuf, never fetches the raw Source Dataset, and
never talks to ClickHouse or Redis directly.
